The model has a fully textured, detailed design that allows for close-up renders. The model was originally modeled in 3ds Max 2017 and rendered with V-Ray 3.6 and Corona 4. Renders have no post-processing or color correction.
Features:

  - high quality model, real-world scaled for an accurate representation of the original object;

  - all materials can be easily modified;

  - model is fully textured with all materials applied;

  - all textures and materials are included and mapped;

  - 3ds Max models are grouped for easy selection, and objects are logically named for ease of scene management;

  - no part-name confusion when importing several models into a scene;

  - no cleaning up necessary;

  - no special plugins needed to open scene;

  - model does not include any backgrounds or scenes used in preview images;

  - model doesn’t include any ngons and triangles;

  - system units: mm.

3d model dimensions: 106 x 5 x 155 mm;
Polycounts:

  - 3dsMax – 14034 polygons, 14025 vertices;

  - fbx – 14160 polygons, 14025 vertices;

  - obj – 28074 polygons, 14025 vertices;

  - stl – 28074 polygons, 14025 vertices;

  - 3ds – 28074 polygons, 25147 vertices.

File Formats:

  - 3ds Max 2014, 3ds Max 2017 + Vray (v3.6);

  - 3ds Max 2014, 3ds Max 2017 + Corona renderer (v4);

  - 3ds Max 2017 + FStorm (v1.5.1c);

  - 3ds Max 2017 with standard material;

  - 3ds, obj, fbx, mtl files.

Textures:
  - model doesn’t include any textures;
Materials:
  - for Corona and Vray. If your version of V-Ray is lower than 3.1, please note: the materials in the BRDF section are worth MicrofasetGTR (GGX). In older versions of Vray, the BRDF field will be blank. Select Blinn, Phong or Ward.

